<title>USA: TABLE - Footstar Q2 shr lower.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Footstar Q2 shr lower.</headline>
<dateline>MAHWAH, N.J. 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p> Oper shr		   $0.50		    $0.58</p>
<p> Oper net		  15,100		   17,900</p>
<p> Sales		    426,000		  419,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  30,400		   30,600</p>
<p>	   6 MONTHS</p>
<p> Oper shr		   $0.66		    $0.61</p>
<p> Oper net		  20,100		   18,000</p>
<p> Sales		    802,900		  755,900</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  30,500		   30,600</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Full company name is Footstar Inc.</p>
<p>1996 sales and net figures are pro-forma adjusted.</p>
<p>Pro forma adjustments consist of the recognition of incremental overhead costs associated with being a stand-alone public company and the elimination of interest income relating to intercompany balances due to the recapitalization of the company pursuant to the October 1996 spin-off of Footstar from Melville Corp, now called CVS Corp.</p>
</text>
